Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Conversion 4 of docs/research-notes/cumulative-coherence-rule-to-check-2026-08-21.md
— the one briefing failure still open. On 2026-08-20 a supervisor A/B
silently came up on the retired Qwen3.5-9B pin; the banner warning was
read only after the run was launched and discarded.

python/carnot/agentic/arc_generator_pin_guard.py:check_frozen_pin reads
the live pin from the ONE canonical constant
(arc_executable_world_model.ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_REPO_SUBSTR — derive,
never duplicate) and refuses a run whose frozen pin differs, naming
both pins and the override. --allow-retired-pin converts the refusal
into a loud not-live-path-evidence warning for deliberate archaeology.
FP rate zero by construction. arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py hoists
its pin to FROZEN_GENERATOR_PIN (build_proposer uses it, the guard
checks it) and calls the guard directly after parse_args. The frozen
pin itself stays 9B on purpose (never-prune).

Mutations: guard equality inverted -> 2 tests RED; harness guard call
removed -> the refuses-before-model-work test no longer refuses (run
had to be killed by timeout: the exact origin failure); restored ->
5/5 GREEN.

The two 20260726 analyzer artifacts recording this harness as a code
dependency were rebuilt per the freshness lint from the same saved
rows. Diff vs committed: ZERO substantive figures moved — only build
timestamps, duration_s, the harness provenance hash, git_head, and the
derived checksum. The rebuild's wholesale rewrite dropped 3-4
hand-written rebuild_note_* keys per artifact; all were restored from
HEAD and the restoration is recorded in
rebuild_note_20260822_pin_guard (never-prune).

